IMPORT prelude

-- Victims of Crime (Financial Assistance Scheme) Act 2022 (Vic) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. The Act counts in years ("within 3 years after", s 23; "within 10 years after",
-- ss 23(4), 36(5), 48(2)(a); "within 6 years after", s 74(2)), in months ("within 6 months", s 27), in days ("within 28
-- days after the day on which notice ... is given", ss 45(2), 46(2)) and by birthdays ("turns 18", "turns 28", "turns 24").
--
-- A period of years or months after a day ends on the same day of the month that many years or months later; where that
-- month has no such day (29 February in a common year, 31 in a 30-day month), on the last day of that month (fork F1).
-- A person "turns" an age on the anniversary of their birth, worked out the same way (a 29 February birthday falls on
-- 28 February in a common year).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Victims of Crime
-- (Financial Assistance Scheme) Act 2022, Version No. 002 (1 December 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of
